+# Plan
+
+## 1. Tests
+
+- [ ] 1.1 Import a dependency with per-condition exports from a module runner for each of six environments in one dev server and snapshot the entry each one gets (packages/vite/src/node/__tests__/environment.spec.ts) [AC-1]
+- [ ] 1.2 Load a JS entry and a CSS entry that both import the dependency in the ssr environment and snapshot the style entry and the default entry (packages/vite/src/node/__tests__/environment.spec.ts) [AC-2]
+- [ ] 1.3 Build each of the six environments with the dependency as input and snapshot the entry each output holds (packages/vite/src/node/__tests__/environment.spec.ts) [AC-3]
+
+## 2. Fix
+
+- [ ] 2.1 Key a package's resolved cache by the resolve options that change an entry, in place of the web/node split (packages/vite/src/node/packages.ts)
+- [ ] 2.2 Pass the resolve options to the cache from the package entry and deep import resolvers (packages/vite/src/node/plugins/resolve.ts)
+- [ ] 2.3 Add the conditions fixture package and link it into the test package (packages/vite/src/node/__tests__/fixtures/test-dep-conditions, packages/vite/src/node/__tests__/package.json, pnpm-lock.yaml)
diff --git a/packages/vite/src/node/__tests__/environment.spec.ts b/packages/vite/src/node/__tests__/environment.spec.ts
new file mode 100644
index 000000000..991eae3e7
--- /dev/null
